 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "Pablo Escobar's hippos are still alive, and Colombia has approved killing some of them.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 5.18
  },
  {
   "text": "In 1981, he imported four.",
   "start": 5.84,
   "end": 7.98
  },
  {
   "text": "His estate lay between Medell\u00edn and Bogot\u00e1.",
   "start": 8.58,
   "end": 10.81
  },
  {
   "text": "After he died in 1993, they escaped and spread.",
   "start": 11.24,
   "end": 14.94
  },
  {
   "text": "Sixteen by 2007, forty by 2014, around two hundred now.",
   "start": 14.94,
   "end": 21.12
  },
  {
   "text": "In April 2026, Colombia approved killing more than eighty of them.",
   "start": 21.96,
   "end": 25.82
  },
  {
   "text": "An Indian billionaire offered to take them to India instead.",
   "start": 26.4,
   "end": 29.04
  },
  {
   "text": "Most conservationists call them invasive; some ecologists disagree.",
   "start": 29.04,
   "end": 33.94
  },
  {
   "text": "So who decides their fate?",
   "start": 34.9,
   "end": 36.22
  }
 ]
